6-Week Progressive Workout Plan: Post-Shoulder Injury Recovery & Muscle Rebuilding
Weekly Schedule Overview
Monday: Upper Body (Shoulder-Safe Focus)
Tuesday: Core & Conditioning
Wednesday: Lower Body & Posterior Chain
Thursday: Active Recovery (Light cardio or yoga)
Friday: Upper Body (Progressive Loading)
Saturday: Core & Full Body Circuit
Sunday: Long Run or Rest

Weeks 1-2: Foundation Phase (Light Weights, High Control)
Monday - Upper Body A
Warm-up: 5 minutes arm circles, band pull-aparts (15 reps), scapular wall slides (10 reps)

Incline Push-ups (hands on bench) - 3×12
Dumbbell Floor Press (limits shoulder extension) - 3×10 at 50% perceived max
Neutral Grip Dumbbell Rows - 3×12 each arm
Band Face Pulls (Peloton bands) - 3×15
Dumbbell Lateral Raises - 3×10 (very light weight, perfect form)
Band External Rotations - 3×15 each arm

Cool-down: Doorway pec stretch, child's pose (2 min)
Tuesday - Core & Conditioning

Dead Bugs - 3×12 each side
Plank - 3×30-45 seconds
Bird Dogs - 3×10 each side
Pallof Press (using bands) - 3×12 each side
Hollow Body Hold - 3×20 seconds
Jump Box Step-ups - 3×15 each leg (no weight)

Finisher: Easy 20-minute run
Wednesday - Lower Body

Goblet Squats (single dumbbell) - 4×12
Romanian Deadlifts (dumbbells) - 3×12
Bulgarian Split Squats - 3×10 each leg
Jump Box Step-downs (eccentric focus) - 3×10 each leg
Single-Leg Glute Bridges - 3×12 each leg
Standing Calf Raises (on box edge) - 3×20

Friday - Upper Body B
Warm-up: Same as Monday

Push-ups (knees if needed) - 3×8-10
Single-Arm Dumbbell Press (on bench) - 3×10 each arm
Renegade Rows (light dumbbells) - 3×8 each arm
Band Pull-aparts - 3×20
Dumbbell Bicep Curls - 3×12
Overhead Tricep Extension (light, careful with shoulder) - 3×10

Saturday - Core Circuit
Complete 3 rounds:

Bicycle Crunches - 20 reps
Russian Twists (medicine ball) - 20 reps
Mountain Climbers - 30 seconds
Side Plank - 30 seconds each side
Medicine Ball Slams - 15 reps
Hanging Knee Raises OR Lying Leg Raises - 12 reps


Weeks 3-4: Building Phase (Moderate Weights, Adding Volume)
Monday - Upper Body A

Standard Push-ups - 3×12-15
Dumbbell Bench Press - 4×10 (increase weight 10-15%)
Single-Arm Dumbbell Rows - 4×10 each arm
Incline Dumbbell Press - 3×10
Band or Dumbbell Face Pulls - 3×15
Lateral Raises Superset with Front Raises - 3×12 each

Tuesday - Core & Conditioning

Weighted Dead Bugs (light dumbbell) - 3×10 each side
Plank with Shoulder Taps - 3×20 taps
Copenhagen Plank (or side plank with leg lift) - 3×20 seconds each
Cable/Band Woodchops - 3×12 each side
Ab Wheel Rollouts (from knees) - 3×8

Consider purchasing an ab wheel ($10-15)


Box Jumps - 3×10

Finisher: Tempo run 25 minutes
Wednesday - Lower Body

Goblet Squats - 4×15 (heavier weight)
Romanian Deadlifts - 4×10 (heavier)
Walking Lunges (holding dumbbells) - 3×12 each leg
Bulgarian Split Squats - 3×12 each leg (add weight)
Nordic Hamstring Curls (assisted) - 3×6

Partner holds ankles or hook feet under couch


Single-Leg Calf Raises - 3×15 each leg

Friday - Upper Body B

Decline Push-ups (feet on bench) - 3×12
Dumbbell Floor Press - 4×8 (heavier weight)
Pendlay Rows (bent-over rows from dead stop) - 4×8
Dumbbell Pullover - 3×12 (careful, start light)
Arnold Press - 3×10
Dumbbell Hammer Curls Superset with Tricep Kickbacks - 3×12 each

Saturday - Full Body Circuit
4 rounds for time:

Burpees - 10 reps
Goblet Squats - 15 reps
Push-ups - 15 reps
Jump Box Jumps - 10 reps
Plank - 45 seconds
Medicine Ball Russian Twists - 30 reps


Weeks 5-6: Strength & Definition Phase
Monday - Upper Body A (Hypertrophy Focus)

Push-ups - 3×15-20
Dumbbell Bench Press - 4×8 (heavy)
Incline Dumbbell Press - 3×10
Dumbbell Flyes - 3×12 (light-moderate, control the stretch)
Bent-Over Dumbbell Rows - 4×8 (heavy)
Face Pulls - 4×20
Lateral Raise Drop Set - 3 sets (12 heavy, 12 medium, 12 light)

Tuesday - Core Strength

Weighted Planks (plate on back) - 3×45 seconds
Hanging Leg Raises - 4×12

Purchase a doorway pull-up bar ($25-40) for this and pull-up progression


Ab Wheel Rollouts - 4×10
Pallof Press - 3×15 each side (heavier band)
Medicine Ball Slams - 4×15
L-Sit Hold (on bench or boxes) - 3×15-30 seconds

Finisher: Hill sprints or intervals
Wednesday - Lower Body Strength

Single-Leg Dumbbell Deadlifts - 4×8 each leg
Goblet Squat Pulses (3 pulses + 1 full rep) - 4×10
Bulgarian Split Squats - 4×10 each (heavy)
Jump Squats (bodyweight) - 3×12
Nordic Hamstring Curls - 3×8
Jump Box Single-Leg Calf Raises - 3×12 each

Friday - Upper Body B (Power & Definition)

Explosive Push-ups (or clap push-ups) - 3×8
Single-Arm Dumbbell Press - 4×8 each (heavy)
Renegade Rows - 4×8 each arm (heavier)
Dumbbell Pullover - 3×12
Dumbbell Curl 21s - 3 sets
Close-Grip Dumbbell Press - 3×12
Band Pull-aparts - 3×25 (burnout)

Saturday - Metabolic Core & Conditioning
5 rounds:

Medicine Ball Slams - 15 reps
Box Jump Overs - 10 reps
Tuck Jumps - 10 reps
V-Ups - 15 reps
Plank to Push-up - 10 reps
Russian Twists - 40 reps


Important Guidelines
Shoulder Safety:

Avoid exercises that cause pain or impingement (overhead pressing behind the neck, wide-grip movements)
Keep shoulder movements in front of your body when possible
If any exercise causes discomfort, regress to an easier variation
Listen to your physical therapist's guidance above all else

Nutrition for Muscle Growth:

Aim for 150-165g protein daily (1g per pound bodyweight)
Eat in a slight caloric surplus (+200-300 calories)
Prioritize post-workout nutrition within 2 hours

Progressive Overload:

Increase weight by 5-10% when you can complete all sets with good form
Add reps before adding weight
Track your workouts in a notebook or app

Recommended Equipment to Purchase:

Ab wheel roller ($10-15)
Doorway pull-up bar ($25-40) - adds major back/core exercises
Resistance band set with door anchor (if Peloton bands aren't sufficient)
Adjustable dumbbells or heavier individual dumbbells as you progress

Recovery:

Keep your Thursday active recovery day - yoga, swimming, or easy 30-min run
Sleep 7-9 hours nightly
Continue running but monitor volume alongside lifting

This plan progressively loads your shoulder while prioritizing chest and core development. The key is patience in the first two weeks to rebuild confidence and movement patterns before pushing harder. Good luck with your recovery and rebuilding!